Cloutier, A. ''et al''. (2019) in their molecular study places ostriches as sister to other palaeognaths, with the rhea as the sister lineage to the remaining, non-ostrich palaeognaths.<ref name="Cloutier2019">{{cite journal |last1=Cloutier |first1=A. |last2=Sackton |first2=T.B. |last3=Grayson |first3=P. |last4=Clamp |first4=M. |last5=Baker |first5=A.J. |last6=Edwards |first6=S.V. |date=2019 |url=https://academic.oup.com/sysbio/article-abstract/68/6/937/5477409?redirectedFrom=fulltext |title=Whole-genome analyses resolve the phylogeny of flightless birds (Palaeognathae) in the presence of an empirical anomaly zone |journal=[[Systematic Biology]]|volume=68 |issue=6 |pages=937–955 |doi=10.1093/sysbio/syz019 |pmid=31135914 |pmc=6857515 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

